##### 8. Assertion Roulette *(Extended Catalog)*
**Affected:** `CalculateTotal_ReturnsCorrectAmount` (line 70)

```csharp
Assert.AreEqual(247.50m, order.TotalAmount);   // no message
Assert.AreEqual(22.28m, order.TaxAmount);       // no message
Assert.AreEqual(269.78m, order.GrandTotal);     // no message
```

**Problem:** 3 assertions, zero message parameters. When one fails, the MSTest output shows `Expected:<247.50> Actual:<0>` with no indication of *which* amount was wrong without reading the stack trace.

**Fix:** Add descriptive messages:
```csharp
Assert.AreEqual(expectedTotal, order.TotalAmount, "TotalAmount (pre-tax subtotal)");
Assert.AreEqual(expectedTax, order.TaxAmount, "TaxAmount (9% tax)");
Assert.AreEqual(expectedGrand, order.GrandTotal, "GrandTotal (subtotal + tax)");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Debugging failures requires reading source code instead of the test output.

