##### 9. Eager Test
**Affected:** `OrderProcessor_FullWorkflow_Succeeds` (line 52)

```csharp
processor.ValidateOrder(order);
processor.CalculateTotal(order);
processor.ApplyDiscount(order, "SAVE10");
processor.ReserveInventory(order);
processor.ProcessPayment(order, new CreditCard("4111111111111111"));
processor.SendConfirmation(order);
processor.UpdateOrderHistory(order);

Assert.AreEqual("Completed", order.Status);
```

**Problem:** 7 distinct production methods called in a single test. If it fails, you can't tell which step caused the failure. Each method deserves its own focused test.

**Fix:** Break into focused tests per behavior, or — if this is meant as an integration/workflow test — mark it explicitly:
```csharp
[TestMethod]
[TestCategory("Integration")]
public void OrderProcessor_FullWorkflow_Succeeds() { ... }
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Failure diagnosis is slow — the single assertion at the end gives no information about which of the 7 steps broke.

